@#==============================================================
#
#  Abs:  Allen-Bradley Remote I/O Scanner Configuration  
#
#  Name: config.ab
#  
#  Rem:  This script is use to configure the
#        Allen-Bradley hardware. To create this file, 
#        first modify the start-up file to run
#        abConfigAuto (<link>).  At the VxWorks prompt 
#        after iocInit do  dbior ("drvAb", 4).  Find the
#        Adapter Status Words.  There are four words
#        (one per group) per adapter. The first word 
#        describes adapter zero, group zero.  Page 5-11 
#        of the AB VMEbus Remote I/O Scanner User's Guide 
#        describes the bits in the status words.  Bits
#        8 and 9 give the adapter size:
#
#            0 for 1/4
#            1 for 1/2
#            2 for 3/4 
#            3 for Full
#
#       Enter the information below for each of the
#       adapters and groups.  Groups are labled 0, 1, 2, 
#       and 3 despite what it looks like in the User's Guide.
#       The format is:
#
#  <rack(= adapter)> <group> <rack size>
#
#  Where rack size is:  1/4, 1/2, 3/4, Full
#
#  
#  Side:  Keep comment lines in this file to 
#         less than 80 chars! 
#
#  Facility:  SLAC/PEPII RF Low-Level RF
#
#  Auth: 12-Mar-1999, K. Luchini     (LUCHINI)
#  Rev:  dd-mmm-yyyy, First Lastname (USERNAME)
#
#--------------------------------------------------------------
#  Mod:
#       dd-mmm-yyyy, First Lastname (USERNAME):
#         comment
#
#==============================================================
#
#  (!! Keep comment lines in this file to less than 80 chars!  Grrrr!)
#
1 0 Full
2 0 3/4
3 0 1/4
